# Versioned MSigDB C3 GMT files (TFT and MIR) fetched by
# regulator-enrichment.qmd. Each render fetches them once when absent, so they
# are a cache rather than an input: the release string in that chapter, not the
# local copy, decides which version an analysis used.
/cache/c3.tft.*.gmt
/cache/c3.mir.*.gmt
# The fetch helper writes a sibling .meta beside each download; without this the
# pair shows up as untracked noise after every render.
/cache/c3.tft.*.gmt.meta
/cache/c3.mir.*.gmt.meta

# Download artifact of the Enrichr example in identifier-utilities.qmd. The
# chunk writes it to a temporary directory now; this keeps an already-present
# copy from showing up as an untracked file.
COVID19_GeneSets.gmt
# Python bytecode from scripts/*.py
__pycache__/

# Review logs live in notes/ and are tracked on purpose; notes/README.md
# explains the directory. They were briefly ignored, which is why the log file
# names still appear in older notes.
